See OpenAI's [Daily Usage Analytics API migration guide](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/enterprise/analytics-api-migration)
for the latest, but as of 2026 you need a workspace-scoped Admin key (not a Platform API key) with
the `enterprise.analytics.usage.read` permission (Enterprise analytics API: Read).

1 - Open the [OpenAI Admin Console](https://admin.openai.com/credentials?tab=admin-keys) under
  **Credentials → Admin keys → Create new admin key**.
  - Choose this workspace, then select **Custom** permissions and set **Enterprise analytics API**
    to **Read**.
  - Reminder: this key can only be viewed/copied once.
2 - Copy the key immediately - you won't see it again; then paste it as the
  `${path_to_instance_parameters}ACCESS_TOKEN` parameter value in the proxy's Secret Manager.

3. After your administrator deploys the Psoxy instance (`terraform apply`), follow the
   `TODO 3 - connect chatgpt-enterprise-analytics in Worklytics.md` file generated in your Terraform
   working directory. That file provides the **Psoxy Base URL** (your proxy/function endpoint),
   which you must enter in the Worklytics connector settings, along with your ChatGPT **Workspace
   Id** (example: `${workspace_id}`), found in the ChatGPT Admin console
   (https://chatgpt.com/admin) on the workspace settings page.
